      <version name="1.1.0" author="Eric Avondo" time="2026-08-17T16:55:05Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[Gain reduction measured through a container, at the audio rate: a compressor that reports nothing can be put in a REAPER container with the panel as the container's last item, or immediately after it, and the reading is then immune to the fader, the panner and the metering preferences; when there is no container, the panel falls back to comparing its own input to the track meter. Compressors recognised by parameter shape first -- a threshold plus a ratio, an explicit makeup, or an attack together with a release -- and by name otherwise, against a list of about fifty device names. StripTease Check.lua can now point at a plugin by hand: it prints the full parameter list and asks which parameter is the makeup, which is the other side, which is the parallel mix, which is the auto-gain switch, and files the answer per plugin type. A parallel mix is undone, so the needle shows the reduction the compressor computes. StripTease Check.lua report rewritten: much shorter, explanations cut back to the essentials, link-recipes section removed. New FX chain StripTease AO The Bus: a worked example of container measurement, for compressors that publish nothing. StripTease.jsfx (StripTease GR) superseded by the panel's own measurement, but still shipped so older projects keep working. Manual: the FX chain table now lists all twelve chains, and the measurement section is rewritten around the two routes.]]></changelog>
