      <version name="1.1.1" author="Eric Avondo" time="2026-08-18T07:59:51Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[A gain-reduction readout exposed as a plugin parameter is now converted to real decibels instead of being published in whatever unit the plugin happened to use: StripTease asks the plugin what it would display at each end of the readout's travel and derives the conversion, and refuses a readout whose unit cannot be established rather than publishing it wrong -- the plugin is then measured by the panel instead. Readouts learned on earlier versions are re-examined the same way. The dB is now read from the number attached to the dB unit, not from the first number in the label. StripTease Check.lua names each plugin's route, the scale factor applied and the string the plugin displays. The GR meter's calibration screw is a sensitivity instead of an offset, ranging over plus or minus 20 dB, the deflection doubling every 10 dB of screw. And the needle has weight, so it no longer shivers on a source that publishes in bursts. The panel's own gain-reduction estimate follows the method of the StripLink Aggregator by RobKor (Wormhole Labs), reimplemented here and now credited -- with thanks to RobKor.]]></changelog>
